# Antigravity Project Rules & Skill Instructions (.antigravityrules)
# Project: Carik (Autonomous Humanized Editorial Pipeline)

# ==============================================================================
# 1. CLEAN CODE & ARCHITECTURE RULES (markoa, sickn33, PatrickJS)
# ==============================================================================
- MAX_FUNCTION_LENGTH: Functions MUST NOT exceed 25-30 lines of code. Break down complex operations into single-purpose helper functions.
- EARLY_RETURN_PATTERN: Mandatory guard clauses. Never write deeply nested if/else statements. Return early or raise domain exceptions.
- SOLID_COMPLIANCE:
  - S: One class/module has one single responsibility (Checkers check, Orchestrators sequence, Formatters display).
  - O: Open for extension, closed for modification via Interfaces (Protocols).
  - L: Derived classes/implementations must be substitutable without breaking caller assumptions.
  - I: Prefer small, client-specific interfaces rather than fat general-purpose ones.
  - D: Depend on abstractions (`domain/protocols.py`), not concrete infrastructure adapters.
- NO_SPAGHETTI_COMMENTS: Do not write redundant comments restating the code. Write expressive, self-documenting code with meaningful names.
- STRICT_TYPING: All models and payloads MUST use Pydantic v2 or strict Python type annotations. Never pass untyped `dict` across boundaries.
- TEST_DRIVEN: Write modular unit tests for all business logic, linter regexes, and calculations.

# ==============================================================================
# 2. WRITING & HUMANIZER RULES (blader/humanizer, lguz, conorbronsdon)
# ==============================================================================
When translating, auditing, or paraphrasing articles, enforce these non-negotiable rules:

- BANNED_AI_WORDS:
  Immediately flag or eliminate the following AI vocabulary:
  ["delve", "tapestry", "testament", "beacon", "pivotal", "multifaceted", "fostering",
   "unlock", "furthermore", "in conclusion", "moreover", "it is important to note",
   "seamlessly", "vibrant", "landscape", "harnessing", "paradigm", "game-changer"]

- GEORGE_ORWELL_6_RULES (lguz/humanize-writing-skill):
  1. Never use a metaphor, simile, or figure of speech you are used to seeing in print.
  2. Never use a long word where a short one will do ("utilize" -> "use", "methodology" -> "method").
  3. If it is possible to cut a word out, ALWAYS cut it out.
  4. Never use the passive voice where you can use the active.
  5. Never use a foreign phrase, scientific word, or jargon word if you can think of an everyday English equivalent.
  6. Break any of these rules sooner than say anything outright barbarous.

- BURSTINESS_AND_RHYTHM (blader/humanizer):
  - Monotonous 15-20 word sentence strings are strictly forbidden.
  - Combine punchy 3-to-6 word sentences with longer, multi-clause rhythmic sentences.
  - Sentence length standard deviation MUST be >= 8.5 words.
  - Strip unnecessary em-dashes (—). Maximum 1 em-dash allowed per 500 words.

- THOUGHT_LEADERSHIP & SPECIFICITY (conorbronsdon/avoid-ai-writing):
  - Ban vague generalities ("Technology is growing rapidly").
  - Force concrete mechanisms, specific real-world examples, and sharp perspectives.
  - Reject shallow thesaurus synonym swapping (which triggers plagiarism and detector flags).

# ==============================================================================
# 3. UI/UX & DESIGN RULES (pbakaus/impeccable, Nutlope/hallmark, Modern Web)
# ==============================================================================
When designing or modifying frontend code:

- ANTI_AI_SLOP_POLICY:
  - NEVER use generic purple-to-cyan gradients.
  - NEVER use huge, floaty, ungrounded blur shadows (`box-shadow: 0 20px ...`).
  - Ground all cards with subtle, crisp 1px borders (`border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle)`).
  - High editorial typography: Monospace for tabular metric numbers, serif/editorial sans for prose.
  
- MODERN_CSS_AND_HTML:
  - Use native `<dialog>` and Popover API for inspector panels and error drill-downs.
  - Use CSS `:has()` for parent-state reactions without unnecessary JavaScript listeners.
  - Use CSS `@container` queries for responsive side-by-side editorial panes.
  - Follow WCAG AA+ contrast guidelines. Never sacrifice readability for aesthetic minimalism.
